#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""locklet: a lock screen for river + rivermonad (or any compositor with
ext-session-lock-v1), in the family of shotlet, waymobar and bgmonad.

  locklet              lock the session
  locklet --preview    show the lock screen in a window without locking
                       (Esc closes it; the password is checked for real)
  locklet idle         run the idle daemon: lock after a while without
                       input, screens off, lock before suspending
  locklet idle pause | resume | toggle | status
  locklet --help

The screen keeps looking the same for an instant (a screenshot taken just
before locking) and then crossfades to the wallpaper bgmonad shows on that
output, blurred, darkened and flowing slowly, with what is playing under the
clock. The password is checked with PAM. Killing locklet does not unlock:
the compositor keeps the session locked until a new locklet unlocks it.
SIGUSR1 unlocks (for scripts).

Settings: ~/.config/locklet/config.json; ~/.config/locklet/style.css is
loaded after the built-in style (GTK CSS) to restyle it.
"""

